# AquariusOS — what this computer does when you switch it on.
#
#   mode=desktop   show the login screen (the normal thing, and the default)
#   mode=game      start straight into Game Mode, like a console
#
# Change it with:  aq game boot on   /   aq game boot off
# Read about it in: docs/restart/game-mode.md
#
# An optional second line, `user=<account>`, says who is logged in when
# mode=game. Without it, the computer picks its first ordinary account, which
# on a one-person machine is the right answer. `aq game boot on` writes it.
#
# ⚠️ THIS COPY IS THE HANDHELD ONE, AND IT SAYS `game` ON PURPOSE.
#
# This file ships as `mode=desktop` on the two desktop images — a PC that
# starts at a login screen, exactly as it always has. The handheld image
# (aquarius-os-handheld, for the ROG Xbox Ally X) ships this copy instead,
# because a handheld with no keyboard that stops at a password box is a brick:
# there is nothing to type a password with.
#
# It is still only a setting. `aq game boot off` puts the login screen back on
# this machine, and if the screen is ever black, Ctrl+Alt+F3 gives you a text
# login from which you can type exactly that.
#
# Plain-language guide: docs/restart/handheld.md
mode=game
